WEBVTT

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.680
You! Run for it! You're in danger!

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:20.930
Oh, jeez! Get going!

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.640
<i>I can't forget that I'm prey too.</i>

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.110
What is that?

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.110
Its mother is in trouble!

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.700
Hey! Get away from there!

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.320
What the hell is this thing?

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.450
Is it part of the tree?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.240
Are they its leaves?

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.840
<i>There are thorns inside...</i>

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.630
<i>and I bet they're full of poison.</i>

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:58.890
<i>Around here, the thing at the top of
the food chain is this tree.</i>

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.930
Look, I know you're sad about it,
but you can't just stand there.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.640
The young, like you,
are always the first to be hunted.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.400
Come on!

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:15.950
Damn it!

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:24.910
Understand? Just stay put.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.580
What? You all came too?

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:36.670
<i>Surviving in this world means
I have to get used to things like this.</i>

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.090
MIMI

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.220
Hey, Mimi.

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.430
Thanks so much.
I was able to keep going because of you.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:45.930
What is that?

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.860
Something I picked up when I was alone,
afraid, and couldn't do anything.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.190
I was suddenly able to find my courage
and felt inspired by it.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.450
I had a cat like this back at home.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.320
Never do anything dangerous
like that again.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.950
You're not cut out for it.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.740
What?

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.130
GRAIN FULL

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.960
You'll die doing it next time.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.800
That's why I can't let you try.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.140
Listen, you don't have to
push yourself like that.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:46.890
But why?

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.140
You encouraged me before, Ango.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.980
Back when we practiced
pulling out the tablecloth,

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.230
you told me that I was actually
capable of doing it myself.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.190
Natsu.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.940
They aren't the same thing.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.240
There was nothing dangerous about that.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.320
But what you just did definitely was.
You could've fallen.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.580
-Got it? From now--
-No way!

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.120
I want to do even more.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.540
This is the first time
that I actually felt useful.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.210
Things I can do,
and even things I can't do,

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.000
I want to push myself and try them all.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.510
-Natsu!
-Ango.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.390
Tell me something, would you have
preferred if she failed just now?

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:27.390
Definitely not.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.220
That's not what I meant.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:32.980
I'm just trying to look out for you...

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:36.810
I know that you don't
consider me an equal, Ango.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.940
Does your arm hurt?

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.780
Did you hit it on something
when we swam earlier?

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:48.240
There's no pain anymore.
It should be mostly healed.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:53.620
It's just, I can't move two of my fingers
and I feel a kind of pain in them.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:00.630
It seems that
I've been hallucinating a lot lately.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.590
Just forget it. Keep moving.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.630
Ryo is above us now.
He's with Semimaru and the rest.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.140
I'll catch up after I rest for a bit.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.140
Go on without me.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.230
I refuse to let us get split up.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.810
We finally found each other
all the way out here.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.650
I was very happy, you know.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:26.070
I absolutely refuse to go by myself
or leave anyone else alone.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:30.070
You just said something
about hallucinating, right?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.200
When we were in the water,

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.040
what exactly did you see?

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:36.910
Did it start before we met?

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:40.750
I was in a cave.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:45.720
I felt like I was traversing through
a deep limestone cave,

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:48.840
even though I know this is a ship.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.220
I was very confused
and pulled the trigger.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.180
I get it. That explains your reaction.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:59.270
You've been through a cave
like that before, haven't you?

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.310
Did something happen to you there?

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.820
Ango, before you assume
you were hallucinating,

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.610
why don't we go check that area?

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.200
If it really exists, then you have
nothing to worry about. Right?

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.660
He's right!

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:18.250
There are many uneven areas
that look just like a limestone cave.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.090
Let's go.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.420
<i>Out of all the people, even these two...</i>

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.430
<i>are starting to feel pity for me now.</i>

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.010
<i>Get it together, Ango!</i>

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.520
It was really cool seeing you
talk back to Ango like that.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:41.600
I actually thought so too.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.690
You've learned how to speak your mind!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.400
Yes, just a little.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:51.280
<i>I've stopped getting replies from Ango.
They must have moved on.</i>

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:54.580
<i>Which means that he isn't having
any problems right now.</i>

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.250
So, yes, this ship
was packed full of guns.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.370
It turned out to be an arsenal.
And there are tons of skeletons.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.000
Oh, really? We haven't seen any.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.290
By the way, how did you end up
carrying a pistol, Ryo?

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.670
Are you, like, an undercover cop?

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:10.680
Semimaru, you mentioned there was
something dangerous earlier.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.010
Did you mean people? Or animals?

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:16.060
Well, I definitely felt
the presence of something before,

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.850
but I don't feel anything right now.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.180
Sorry, I think it was just my imagination.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.480
Are you crazy, Semmy?

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.860
That means you almost shot Ryo
over nothing! You big dummy! I hate you!

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.070
<i>I can't be sure it's just nothing.</i>

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:30.320
<i>Semimaru is stupid,
but he has good instincts.</i>

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:31.900
Matsuri.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:34.870
Take Semimaru back along the path
we took and get out of here.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:37.030
I'm going further down to pick up Ango.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.370
Good joke!

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.250
I'm not leaving here empty-handed.

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.750
We know Natsu and Arashi are okay now,
so let's just take it easy.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.670
It sure is tough moving directly upwards.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:55.600
But we still need to go even higher
to reach the control room.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:58.260
Perhaps there's a ladder or something?

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:01.680
After all, it seems like this ship was
designed to be vertical.

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.520
That's true.
I'm certain they would have included one.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.020
I'll look for it.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:10.860
Well, we've got plenty of time.
Let's take this easy and not rush.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:14.450
There's half a day
until the missiles are supposed to launch.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.950
Hey! Check that out!

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.330
A basketball hoop?

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:25.370
Balls, jump ropes, dumbbells,
and even a bowling set!

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:28.290
Are those golf clubs? How ridiculous!

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:30.380
Oh, boy. I think we hit the jackpot!

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:32.050
Here it goes, Matsuri!

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.260
That hurt, Matsuri!

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.260
You're too slow!

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:41.640
All right, we're taking this whole set!

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.310
Next Sunday we're having
a ping pong competition!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.190
<i>What do they think they're doing?</i>

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:48.730
<i>What did they even come here for?</i>

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:55.740
Say, Semmy.
Doesn't it feel kind of weird in here?

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:58.320
-What?
-If we had found this way earlier,

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.660
it would've been so nostalgic,

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:04.410
I think I would have started crying from
how much it made me miss the old world.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:10.500
But now, I totally feel like I could
keep on living without any of this stuff.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:13.170
I think I get you.

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:17.720
It's like getting used to sleeping alone
after your boyfriend dumps you, right?

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.930
Now's not the time for dirty jokes, Semmy!

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:23.390
Anyway, that's the kind of feeling
I get when I'm here.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.020
I'm glad we decided to come.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.060
<i>She's glad we came?</i>

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:34.070
This is definitely a cave.
It's really dark.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.240
Ango, is this the place you meant?

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.110
I'm not sure if it's exactly the same.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.660
But it felt just like this,
which means that I wasn't hallucinating.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.750
<i>I was seriously starting to think
I had lost my mind.</i>

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.330
<i>I really should trust myself more.</i>

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.090
Bodies!

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.630
There are many of these
lying around the ship.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.130
What are these bumps?

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:56.630
Don't touch it, Arashi.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.930
You know, I've seen similar stuff before,
in footage taken underwater.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:05.770
For example, in footage of the Titanic
or other sunken ships,

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.600
the wreckage often ends up all lumpy
like this, right?

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:12.110
If I had to guess,
it's from a bacteria that eats iron.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.780
Apparently, they get energy
from oxidizing iron.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:19.740
Originally, they couldn't survive
in the atmosphere,

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:21.820
so these must have evolved.

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:28.540
There's plenty of iron in humans as well.
Mainly in our blood.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:35.250
Basically, I imagine the crew of the ship
died in a very bloody manner.

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:39.590
Then the bacteria multiplied
in the iron of the blood.

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.600
Relax. It's not like
they're going to start jumping at us.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.010
If my assumption is accurate,

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.520
this ship will just deteriorate
until nothing is left.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:53.810
Most of the things on Earth get recycled.
Humans included.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:55.860
Say, Ango,

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.030
were you ever a student council president
or captain of a team?

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:01.860
Or maybe you had younger siblings?

00:11:02.570 --> 00:11:04.280
No. Why?

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:06.740
Because you always answer
whenever we ask a question.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.370
It never gets on your nerves.

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:10.330
Are you saying you find that convenient?

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:12.000
Not at all.

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:13.670
I'm trying to say I find it very cool.

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:17.590
From my perspective, you're like a person

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.090
who stands up front
and takes the brunt of the wind.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:23.640
There's nothing cool about me whatsoever.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.140
I'm pathetic.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:28.930
What? What is that over there?

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:30.230
A countdown?

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:32.940
Oh, I saw that in some other places too.

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:34.610
What does "final day" mean?

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:39.280
Presumably, it was a countdown to the end
of humanity, when the meteorite fell.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.070
-Let's move.
-Oh, right!

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:56.210
We finally made it to the control room.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.420
It's all thanks to the ladder
you found, Hotaru.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.050
It was a real surprise.

00:12:01.510 --> 00:12:04.640
It turns out there are many built into
the floors and walls of the whole ship.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:09.220
Okay. For now, let's see if we can
shut down that missile they talked about.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.850
And the self-destruct.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:12.850
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:14.810
The countdown is still going.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:17.230
I'll try and put a stop to it.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.440
ACTION CANNOT BE EXECUTED.
THE TIME WINDOW HAS PASSED.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.030
You can't cancel it?

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:24.410
It won't let me input commands.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:30.620
So then, in 12 hours, a bunch of missiles,
including a nuclear one,

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.500
will launch and rain down on all of Japan?

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:36.460
And lastly, this ship will self-destruct.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:41.170
But don't you think there must be
another way for us to put a stop to it?

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.510
You're right.
Let's find an operations manual.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:44.800
Sure.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.850
<i>I really want to believe that we have
nothing to worry about.</i>

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:52.520
<i>But what if
there's even a slight chance...</i>

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.770
Is it just me or did it get
really dark in here suddenly?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.570
Maybe it's short on power

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.570
and is shutting down to conserve it.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:05.650
Hey, now!

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:08.030
Something is moving down below us!

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:10.330
Is the ship going to rotate back again?

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:13.160
Over there!
The sound is really loud over that way.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.290
What's up with this place?

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:18.170
There's a huge hole over here!

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:21.920
It looks like it goes all the way up
and all the way down.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:25.510
Look at this, Semmy.
This whole thing might be an elevator.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:27.640
An elevator? Really?

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.720
But there isn't any door,
and we can see through it.

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.310
So this is what elevators are like?

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:34.390
Hold on, Ryo.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:39.770
Don't tell me that you've never ridden
on an elevator before.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:40.690
Not once.

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.360
-You've never seen one either?
-No.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:43.690
Seriously?

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:48.490
Ryo, I'm really starting to
feel sorry for you.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.790
What do you think this sound
we've been hearing is?

00:13:58.210 --> 00:14:00.380
It doesn't look like there are
any paths leading up.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.880
But it seems that the bacteria
hasn't eaten away at this area much.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:06.720
There's a map here.

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:07.680
YOU ARE HERE

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:10.640
Is that where we are? We're so far down.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.930
It's still a long way to the surface.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:17.020
We need to find or force our way through
somehow to get topside.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:21.610
<i>The ship's crew must have understood
how all of this worked.</i>

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.980
<i>If all those people have died,</i>

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:28.360
<i>then it means all the technology
was lost with them.</i>

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.280
It's wider up ahead.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:32.240
It looks like we can go upward.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.950
-Awesome! Let's go, Natsu.
-Right!

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.000
No way!

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:40.830
It's moving fast!

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:43.920
The iron-eating bacteria is
spreading all over the place!

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.840
They seemed totally dormant before!

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:53.430
Something must have changed
as a result of us coming in.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:56.680
You mean like, they were sleeping
and we woke them up?

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:57.980
Let's leave now.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:02.020
They might cause the ship's systems
to malfunction somehow.

00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:03.270
-Right!
-Right!

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:17.200
Are you okay, Ryo?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.200
So, how does it look?

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.540
There's a way out
about 50 or 60 meters down,

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.080
but we don't have enough rope.

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:26.050
So, what do we do?

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:31.720
What the hell was that?
Some kind of black blob just shot up.

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.430
That noise we were hearing earlier
must have been that thing moving.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.810
I still hear some noise below,
so there might be more coming.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:43.600
Then the system is focusing
the remaining power on moving those.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.400
Wait a second!

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:49.900
There's nobody on this ship,
so why is it doing this on its own?

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.400
-Matsuri.
-What?

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.620
Do you have anything I can eat
to help me forget my fear?

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:58.740
I've got some of the dumplings
you made this morning.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.210
Would you like some, Ryo?

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.340
No.

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:10.800
But why are they in this shape?
Aren't dumplings round? Are these drops?

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:14.260
They're not drops.
They're dumplings made for moon-viewing.

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.510
But those are normally round.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.760
At my house, they were like this.

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:20.770
Really? Is that how you do it in Shizuoka?

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:23.230
I don't know about anybody else,
but that's how my mom did it.

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:24.900
Where was your mother from?

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:26.610
Kansai.

00:16:26.690 --> 00:16:29.690
My mom didn't really do events,

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:32.400
but she would always celebrate
the star festival and moon viewing.

00:16:32.860 --> 00:16:34.320
But only when I was really little.

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.530
Your mom was a romanticist.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:37.450
What?

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:40.790
I mean, both of those are holidays
where we look up at the night sky.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.420
Then maybe she had some
fond memories of those with my dad.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.630
That reminds me, did you know your father?

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:53.380
No. She never told me who he was,
no matter how much I asked.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:58.180
But why the hell did she keep it a secret
until the end? He's my father!

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:01.430
At the very least, she could have told me
before I ended up here!

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:04.270
You are keeping a secret.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:07.400
You are debating
as to whether to share it.

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.360
I think it's because your mom was kind.

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:12.570
She never told you

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:16.070
because she wasn't sure if knowing
would affect you positively or negatively.

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.070
The only one who can decide
what impact it has is me!

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.530
That's my problem to deal with.

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:23.450
I should be the one who gets to decide,
not my mother!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:26.040
I want the chance
to know more about myself!

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:29.080
Semimaru, you said something before
in the sauna.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:30.670
What did you mean by that?

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:35.380
"Humans are the happiest
when they feel regret."

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:36.930
I said that?

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:38.050
Yes, you did.

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:41.060
I guess I've been saying
some pretty clever stuff.

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:45.560
Well, this doesn't apply to
every regret in the world,

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:48.020
since there are some
you just can't help but have.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:53.150
But for example, those times when someone
gets hurt because of something you did,

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:56.150
it can make you pretty egotistical.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.860
What do you mean by "egotistical"?

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:04.450
I mean, thinking about
how you had an impact on someone's life

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.830
usually feels great.

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:09.880
And when you're gloomy because of regret,

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.750
you don't have to bother with
anything else.

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.800
In the end, the most stressful times are

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.340
when you have to whip yourself into shape
and get moving again, you know.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:25.390
Okay! I've got some food in my stomach,
so let's get out of here!

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:28.560
What the...

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:31.230
It seems like we're stuck here
because of the brake.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:34.230
Doing this will lower us little by little.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.150
Stop it, you idiot!
We'll drop straight down!

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:43.490
Relax! Just look, it's started to lower
at a steady pace.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.080
Look. There's our way out.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.040
Matsuri, go! Semimaru!

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.710
Okay, just let me move the ping pong--

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:00.010
Semmy!

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.760
No...

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.060
Help me out, Matsuri!

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:20.860
When did you... put the rope...

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:25.700
Listen up! You need to stop acting
like a conceited punk

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:27.540
who does whatever he wants

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:31.790
and expects to get out of it alive,
because next time you won't!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.580
I'm sorry...

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:36.920
I'm sorry.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:38.510
<i>Why...</i>

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.670
-I'm so sorry!
-<i>did I save him?</i>

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.310
We should be able to climb up from here.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:52.310
There are plenty of footholds
and places for support.

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:55.400
We're going to climb? Here? By ourselves?

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.610
We'll all be connected to one rope.

00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:02.450
We can help each other climb up gradually.
Just follow after me.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:07.490
I'll take the lead.
Your right hand is still injured, Ango.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:09.200
I've got the lead.

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:12.830
<i>I can't move two of my fingers.</i>

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.170
<i>But I'll manage.</i>

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:19.000
<i>This time I'll make it
to the top and get out of here.</i>

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.380
<i>Along with Shigeru.</i>

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.800
Okay. You're next, Natsu.

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:28.390
Just start by climbing up to me.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.520
I'll help pull you up from here.

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:32.480
Just stay calm and go slow.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:46.870
This is seawater. Did it flood in here?

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:49.910
There's a bunch of that
liquid concrete algae.

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:51.370
Well, I think we should...

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:56.170
I'll keep my mouth shut.
I won't get cocky anymore. Sorry, my bad.

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:00.000
What is this stuff?

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.510
Soybeans? And they're sprouting!

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:04.930
Aren't those just bean sprouts?

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:07.640
When soybeans sprout,
they're bean sprouts.

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:09.180
I've heard about this.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.890
There was research where they grew plants
on film sheets without using soil.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:16.690
Places like these are pretty much perfect
for cultivating them.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:18.520
It looks like they just sprouted.

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:22.400
And they were able to do it
all on their own.

00:21:22.860 --> 00:21:24.030
But isn't this seawater?

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:28.070
They must have adapted to the environment
over time to be able to grow in seawater.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:32.830
Plants are capable of
changing their own makeup like that.

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:35.080
There's nothing else in the world

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:39.000
that's as tough and determined to thrive
as plants, I'm telling you!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:41.170
So you're a really big fan of them?

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:43.340
Because I'm the daughter of a farmer.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:45.970
Anyway, I'm going to
try to cultivate these beans.

00:21:46.090 --> 00:21:48.260
Semmy, help me gather up
as many as we can take!

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:51.050
Seriously? We're already full.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:54.770
It looks like this is a dead end,
although I do see a door over there.

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:57.350
Damn it!

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:00.020
Fine, I'll do it.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:02.270
Heave-ho!

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:06.030
I'll gather them all up!
All the beans! Every last one!

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.610
Wow! You're the best, Semmy!

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:10.450
-But you're right, beans are great.
-Awesome!

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:12.620
I just can't figure these two out.

00:22:12.700 --> 00:22:14.790
-The king of all beans!
-You're silly!

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.660
So, this is where that loud noise
we heard earlier was coming from.

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:22.090
FINAL DAY: TIME REMAINING

00:22:22.670 --> 00:22:24.300
Hey, something's moving over there.

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:35.680
Hey, guys, wasn't that a missile
that just passed us?

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:45.480
<i>Even though they know it's dangerous,</i>

00:22:46.070 --> 00:22:48.320
<i>they have no other choice
but to come here for water.</i>

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:54.580
<i>If some of them are sacrificed,
then others can survive.</i>

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:57.830
<i>That's one of the merits
of being part of a herd.</i>

00:22:58.870 --> 00:23:02.630
<i>Then, I wonder how each of those
who is sacrificed feels.</i>

00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:06.880
<i>I'm sure my father and the others
thought the same.</i>

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:11.640
<i>It was okay if they died, so long as
it meant someone else survived.</i>

00:23:12.760 --> 00:23:14.720
<i>Even if they weren't saved,</i>

00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:20.980
<i>it was all right
because I was going to survive.</i>

00:23:29.740 --> 00:23:30.990
I fell asleep.

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:33.370
Wait! Is everyone still okay?

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:44.960
What's that?

00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:48.670
Is that fire?
